WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.322 --> 00:00:04.038
(atmospheric music)

00:00:04.038 --> 00:00:07.590
- Jetliners are basically flying homes.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:09.634
It's a sealed pressure canister.

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:12.130
It's incredibly strong.

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:14.880
It will last practically forever.

00:00:18.016 --> 00:00:19.885
I'm Bruce Campbell, and you're inside

00:00:19.885 --> 00:00:22.552
the cockpit area of my 727 home.

00:00:24.227 --> 00:00:26.015
I can appreciate that
some folks might feel

00:00:26.015 --> 00:00:28.929
a bit isolated or that it
might simply strike them

00:00:28.929 --> 00:00:31.066
as an unusual living environment.

00:00:31.066 --> 00:00:34.317
But for me, it's always
felt completely natural.

00:00:34.317 --> 00:00:36.859
(playful music)

00:00:36.859 --> 00:00:39.320
The entry is via the aft airstairs,

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.120
which are retractable and are retracted

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.777
whenever I leave for an extended time.

00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:47.958
The aft area of the aircraft
now is my living space.

00:00:47.958 --> 00:00:51.964
My very primitive shower is located there.

00:00:51.964 --> 00:00:56.550
The two natural aft lavatories
are both functional.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:57.838
Sleeping quarters are there, in the form

00:00:57.838 --> 00:00:59.847
of a simple futon sofa.

00:00:59.847 --> 00:01:03.678
And a bench, where I spend
lots of time embellishing

00:01:03.678 --> 00:01:05.761
elements of the aircraft.

00:01:08.589 --> 00:01:11.817
Jetliners retire at the
rate of about three per day.

00:01:11.817 --> 00:01:14.406
For the most part, I think we shred them.

00:01:14.406 --> 00:01:16.902
And then we spin around 180 degrees

00:01:16.902 --> 00:01:20.037
and make a home, after
having just shredded

00:01:20.037 --> 00:01:23.322
an aerospace class home sized structure.

00:01:23.322 --> 00:01:25.122
If you were an
extraterrestrial looking down

00:01:25.122 --> 00:01:27.455
on this behavior, you'd
wonder whether this species

00:01:27.455 --> 00:01:31.252
has all its marbles in place or not.

00:01:31.252 --> 00:01:34.584
(evocative classical music)

00:01:34.584 --> 00:01:37.336
People have asked me
whether it crashed here,

00:01:37.336 --> 00:01:39.971
and I simply restored the wreck.

00:01:39.971 --> 00:01:41.341
That's an odd thing to hear.

00:01:41.341 --> 00:01:43.674
It's completely impractical.

00:01:45.764 --> 00:01:47.390
Next time you're in a jetliner,

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:49.561
close your eyes for a moment, in your mind,

00:01:49.561 --> 00:01:51.941
remove all the seats
and all the other people

00:01:51.941 --> 00:01:54.983
and then open your eyes with that vision

00:01:54.983 --> 00:01:58.280
and consider the expanse
of the living room.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:01.447
It's a good environment, it really is.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:05.070
(birds chirping)

